{
	"comment": "Shared conformance vectors for order keys: engine/fractional (Go) and client/src/fractional.ts with client/src/ordering.ts (TypeScript) must make the same key from the same bounds, so a key a server-side writer makes and a key a browser makes sit correctly in one list. null bounds are open: before-first, after-last, or the first key of an empty list. `between` pins one key between two bounds; `nBetween` pins n keys; `actorBetween` pins the actor-suffixed key a client writes into a movable list (order_field), with the actor read as UTF-16 code units. `rejects` lists bounds both sides must refuse: `invalidKey` for a bound that is not an order key, `outOfOrder` for a lower bound that does not sort below the upper one. Each `walks` entry starts from an empty list and inserts one key per gap index (clamped to the list length, so 0 prepends and a large index appends) between that gap's neighbors, with the actor-suffixed key when `actor` is set; `want` is the list after the last insert, which must also be strictly ascending.",
